# LR-CC2: CC2 ground state plus an excited state, for helium.
#
# `calc_type lrcc2` runs the CC2 ground state and then linear-response CC2 on
# top, so the results span three tasks: scf, cc2 (with excitations[]), and the
# MP2 energy computed along the way.
#
# `iter_max 2` caps the CC2 iterations; a production run would leave it at the
# default. It does NOT make this case cheap: the constant-part construction
# dominates and is not bounded by iter_max, so the run still takes ~30 min on 20
# threads. That is why this case is tagged `verylong` -- do not be tempted to
# retier it on the assumption that the iteration cap bounds the cost.
#
# Fixed `k`, no `protocol` ladder: the correlated step takes the reference at a
# single resolution, and one that climbed the ladder mixes resolutions and aborts
# in the tensor layer.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc --wf=cc2 lrcc2_he_excited.in)

dft
    xc       hf
    k        5
    maxiter  10
    econv    1e-5
    dconv    1e-3
end

cc2
    freeze     0
    calc_type  lrcc2
    iter_max   2
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    He  0.0  0.0  0.0
end
